<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- The simulator's securityd gates the keychain on the
     application-identifier entitlement: without one, every SecItemAdd answers
     errSecMissingEntitlement (-34018) and each credential the editor saves is
     dropped at the door. This file is embedded in the app executable's
     __TEXT,__entitlements section (with its DER form in __TEXT,__ents_der) at
     link time - the simulator runtime reads entitlements from there, and the
     host kernel, which refuses restricted entitlements in an ad-hoc code
     signature, never sees them. The prefix is not a team: the simulator
     checks the entitlement's presence and shape, not a certificate chain. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>application-identifier</key>
    <string>UBIQUITTY.org.ubiquitty.Ubiquitty</string>
    <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>UBIQUITTY.org.ubiquitty.Ubiquitty</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
